The partition remains 2,500 mm high × 100 mm deep, with 1,800 mm of air above it; “storey-scale” does not mean 
increasing its envelope.
Keep all partition glass between 450 and 2,100 mm unobstructed.
The carpet stays level through the room; a partition base is a narrow vertical frame, never a raised room platform.
The stair helix is cut into the solid core, rather than made opaque on cage glass, to retain the outer walking annulus 
sightline.
Keep the existing stair core/tread/rail/cage radii of 800 / 2,600 / 2,630 / 2,750 mm.

Keep [Glass_Clear](../../../../docs/systems/GLASS.md) near-clear, with one broad and one thin translucent diagonal 
streak.
Near-black values belong in cut reveals and grazing edges, without making the panes mirror-dark.
Dark figures are visible in the concept views; this is a visual review of still images, not proof of gameplay 
readability through two panes.

