CORE IDENTITY
01  ART-DIRECTION NORTH STAR

The project should look like an optimistic corporate future designed around 1999–2003 rather than a contemporary 
sci-fi world dressed in retro references. The visual language is clean, cool, sharply designed and intentionally 
artificial. The world is aspirational on the surface: white towers, blue skies, immaculate signage, glass, brushed 
metal and luminous office light. The game itself then abuses that immaculate world with slapstick PvP chaos.
The key contrast is deliberate: the environment is airy and architecturally clean, while characters are graphic, 
exaggerated and immediately readable. The result should feel like an early-2000s design agency built the city, a 
fashion illustrator designed the employees, and then somebody started a workplace war.
THE SHORTEST POSSIBLE BRIEF
2001 corporate futurism outside. Sharp graphic lawyers inside. Clean enough to feel expensive; strange enough to feel 
fictional; simple enough to read during chaos.

