+
+The wall revisions addressed the numeral's raised reading, missing helix, missing red leaf and overgrown stair 
context.
+The façade, ceiling and partition revisions addressed meeting-box height, roof-like mass and missing supporting stair 
cues.
+Every exact initial/revision prompt and selected output is recorded in [prompts_r4.json](prompts_r4.json); retained 
discarded attempts have `try_01_r4.png` / `try_02_r4.png` names inside their family folders.
+Reference-board and contact-sheet assembly are deterministic image layouts, not extra ImageGen tries.
+
+Selected sheets were inspected visually for distinct A/B forms, two interior positions, secondary street insets, era 
cues, hard shadow edges, open circulation, low meeting frames and figure contrast.
+Small painted reliefs, camera height/distance, exact frame depth, glass strength and the inward reading of 
white/cobalt edges remain perspective approximations; do not infer measurements from the paintings.
+Small street insets simplify details and sometimes repeat the painted floor code; a build must use its actual 
per-floor code rather than copy that incidental repetition.
+Two-pane visibility is an art-review target illustrated by the stills, not a measured gameplay result.
+
+Read-only validation uses `Get-FileHash -Algorithm SHA256` against the 28 pre-existing non-log 
brief/round-1/round-2/round-3 files and `[System.Drawing.Image]::FromFile(...)` for PNG dimensions.
+Final dimensions and preservation results are recorded in [validation_r4.json](validation_r4.json).
+No automated tests, Unity compile, Play Mode, multiplayer or performance checks were run for this artwork task.
+All task-authored files remain in this folder tree; rounds 1–3 and all briefs are retained unchanged, with no 
state-changing git commands.
+
+**Next:** Alex reviews the five directions before any kit modelling.

